# Key material for the Node build-tree cache in .github/workflows/ios.yml.
#
# The tree -- the unpacked Node source plus out/, objects included -- is the part
# of a device build that costs hours, so CI caches it and reuses it. Only its
# SHA-256 enters the cache key, which is why this file exists at all: a reader can
# see what a bump means without decoding a hash.
#
# Bump the line below when the tree must not be reused:
#
#   * Node's version moves (different sources, different objects);
#   * `prepare-engine.sh` changes the *layout* of what it stages inside the tree;
#   * the compiler wrapper changes in a way `wrapper_version` in that script does
#     not already cover.
#
# A patch-set change does NOT need a bump: the tree records the patch set it was
# built from and restores its own pristine sources before re-applying. Editing
# this file is the deliberate, rare invalidation; a stale tree would otherwise
# cost two hours to discover.
tree-3 node-24.22.3
